# Default programming workflow: pstack

For any nontrivial engineering work in this environment (features, bugs, refactors,
perf, architecture, investigations that lead to code, PR babysitting, shipping),
route through **pstack `/poteto-mode`** as the default workflow.

## When it applies

- New behavior, bug fix, refactor, performance work, or multi-step verification
- "How does X work?" / "why was Y built this way?" before changing code
- Design forks that need architect / arena / interrogate
- Opening, babysitting, or landing PRs

## When it does not apply

- Pure casual Q&A with no rigor needed
- User explicitly opts out ("skip poteto", "just edit", "quick one-liner")
- Mechanical one-file typos the user already specified verbatim

## How to apply

1. Read and follow the `poteto-mode` skill (plugin: pstack) before implementing.
2. Match a playbook; copy its steps into the session todo list.
3. Spawn playbook subagents with `subagent_type: "poteto-agent"` unless a routed
   skill (`how`, `why`, `interrogate`, `reflect`, `swarm`, `arena`, `architect`)
   prescribes another type.
4. Honor `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` for per-role Task models.
5. For this repo, prove user-facing changes with
   `.cursor/skills/verify-signal-diagnosis-agent` when the change touches CLI,
   API, Web UI, or diagnosis service behavior. Do not claim RealLLM product
   verification without credentials.
6. Respect frozen V0.2 contracts in `AGENTS.md` / `docs/CONTRACTS_V0_2.md`: no
   silent product behavior changes, no ScriptedPlanner product fallback, no
   rewriting accepted evaluation or Demo assets.
7. **Strong-model work never silently falls back to the parent/default model.**
   Roles that pstack routes to judgment/prose/hardest models (including
   adversarial review of designs and implementation plans, `interrogate`,
   architect synthesis when those roles require a strong model) must use the
   configured strong model. If that Task fails (usage limit, spend cap, model
   unavailable), **stop that judgment pass**, give the operator a paste-ready
   Codex/external-strong-model brief with PR/commit links, and wait. Do not
   complete the strong-review deliverable yourself on the parent/default model
   and present it as the strong-model result. Mechanical docs edits and
   applying an already-returned Codex critique remain allowed on the parent.

